After[ breakfast] climb the 5th century Sigiriya rock fortress which is a world heritage site, built by King Kashy[apa (477]-[495] AD). The 'Lion Rock' is a[ cit]adel of unusual beauty rising 200 meters from the scrub jungle. The rock[ was] the innermost stronghold of the 70 hectare fortified town. Visit the world-renowned frescoes of the 'Heavenly Maidens' of Sigiriya, which are in a sheltered pocket of the rock approached by a spiral stairway. These frescoes are painted in earth pigments on plaster.
